1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:01,260
W: Is anything the matter?

2
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:02,900
You don't look well.

3
00:00:03,175 --> 00:00:04,460
M: My tooth is bothering me.

4
00:00:04,920 --> 00:00:06,625
I think I'd better get it checked out.

5
00:00:07,220 --> 00:00:13,600
Do you think it would be okay if I leave the office a bit early this afternoon to drop by a dentist's office near my place?

6
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:19,150
W: Sure, that will be fine as long as you finish the weekly report before you take off.

7
00:00:19,660 --> 00:00:30,400
Remember, the meeting with the general manager is scheduled to start tomorrow morning at 9 o'clock, and I've asked Ted Bradley to look over the figures to make sure there aren't any errors in them.

8
00:00:30,720 --> 00:00:31,260
M: Sure thing.

9
00:00:31,425 --> 00:00:34,560
I am just about done here, so he should get it before lunch.
